      "writtenOn": "2022-12-29T22:51:38Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think, we can omit having enums if we leave the only place in code where we get positional parameters (excluding the parameter with index 0—the effect descriptor, I think for it we should have a constant so we can easily distinguish it from other zeroes).\n\nFor example, in this particular test, we can provide a function which fills out an instance of `DynamicsProcessing::EngineArchitecture` from the parameter tuple—the code which is currently in the test name formatter. We can replace individual fields in the `DynamicsProcessingTestEngineArchitecture` fixture with a field of the `DynamicsProcessing::EngineArchitecture` type, too. I think, that should work.",
      "parentUuid": "456c818a_62c390b8",
      "range": {
